==History==
2016
*The Ice Wizard [[Cards|card]] was added to the game on 29/2/2016, in the [[Version History#March%202016%20Update%20(29/2/2016)|March 2016 Update]].
*On 23/3/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (23/3/2016)|Balance Update]], increased the Ice Wizard's damage by 5%.
*On 3/5/2016, the [[Version History#May%202016%20Update%20(3/5/2016)|May 2016 Update]], decreased the {{Rarity|Legendary}} card Level cap to 5 (from 6) and fixed the "range bug" and decreased the Ice Wizard's range to 5.5 tiles (from 6 tiles), but his effective range is unchanged. Also, this update changed his description. It used to read, "''This chill caster hails from the far North. He shoots ice shards at enemies, slowing down their movement and attack speed.''". His sound effects were also changed.
*On 4/7/2016, the [[Version History#Tournaments%20Update%20(4/7/2016)|Tournaments Update]], allowed the [[Elixir Collector]] to be affected by the Ice Wizard's slowing.
*On 24/8/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (24/8/2016)|Balance Update]], decreased the Ice Wizard's hitpoints by 5%.
2017
*On 11/8/2017, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (11/8/2017)|Balance Update]], increased the Ice Wizard's damage by 10% and increased his attack time interval to 1.7 seconds (from 1.5 seconds).
2018
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Ice Wizard from Spell Valley to Frozen Peak.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Legendary}} cards start at Level 9 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 5).
*On 1/10/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (1/10/2018)|Balance Update]], increased the Ice Wizard's slowdown duration to 2.5 seconds (from 2 seconds). This change was voted for by the community.
*On 3/12/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/12/2018)|Balance Update]], decreased the Ice Wizard’s hitpoints by 11% and increased his damage by 10%.
2019
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], added a card render to the Ice Wizard's card info screen.
2020
*On 7/7/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (7/7/2020)|Balance Update]], changed the Ice Wizard's card render.
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], decreased the Ice Wizard's hitpoints by 3%.
*On 10/6/2021, a [[Version History#Maintenance Break (10/6/2021)|maintenance break]], decreased the Ice Wizard's hitpoints by 0.1%. This was to fix a rounding error where a Level 12 Fireball should've been able to kill an equivalent Level Ice Wizard.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
*On 7/12/2021, the [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(7/12/2021)|2021 Quarter 4 Update]], allowed the Ice Wizard to deal Spawn Damage with a slow effect.
2022
*On 30/3/2022, the [[Version History#Miner%20Update%20(30/3/2022)|Miner Update]], changed the Ice Wizard's sound effects. Previously, his sound effects when deployed were identical to those of the [[Zap]].
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Ice Wizard from Frozen Peak to Spooky Town.
2023
*On 6/6/2023, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/6/2023)|Balance Update]], increased the Ice Wizard's spawn area radius to 3 tiles (from 2.5 tiles). 
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14). 
2024
*On 6/8/2024, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/8/2024)|Balance Update]], increased the Ice Wizard's area radius to 1.5 tiles (from 1 tile).
2025
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], decreased the Ice Wizard's damage by 1.11% and increased his spawn damage by 1.2%.
*On 6/10/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/10/2025)=|Balance Update]] decreased the slowdown effect to -30% (from -35%).

